# Applies to `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .` (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore
# next to the Dockerfile before falling back to <context>/.dockerignore).
# Keep the context small and, above all, keep local state and secrets OUT of the image.
.git
.github
.venv
.audit
.crb
.env
deploy/.env
deploy/secrets
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/node_modules
ui/dist
tests/.cache
coverage.xml
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.jsonl
docs
# ...except the Markdown the UI bundles at build time: the eight guides and the decision records
# (ui/src/help/docs.ts, ui/src/help/adrs.ts). Without them the image's Help could open no
# guide at all (docs/PREVENTION.md P-051); the runtime stage copies only ui/dist, so none of
# these files is in the final image as a file. `vite build` refuses a context without them.
!docs/*.md
!docs/adr/*.md
scripts
data
